SUMMARY:[projected] scMethyl methods manuscript — bioRxiv preprint + jour
 nal submission (day unknown — verify)
STATUS:TENTATIVE
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:Closes May 2027 (day unknown)\n\nDAY NOT KNOWN. This is pinned 
 to the first of the month so it is visible\, not because it is due then. F
 ind the real date before you plan around it.\n\nCycle 2027\n\nThe single h
 ighest-leverage asset for AMCAS\, Hertz and PD Soros. A first-author or co
 -first methods paper preprinted by mid-2028 is what the whole Fall 2028 st
 ack is built on\, and posting to bioRxiv 6-12 months before acceptance cou
 nts on AMCAS Work and Activities. Under Scenario A this MUST be submitted 
 before leaving for Oxford\, with revisions managed remotely. Push for firs
 t or co-first — middle author on lab papers does not move the needle. IP
  NOTE: in the US a public disclosure (talk\, poster\, or preprint) starts 
 a 12-month clock to file\, and most other jurisdictions have no grace peri
 od at all. Talk to Broad OSAP BEFORE the preprint\, not after.\n\nRe-confi
 rm by 2026-10-01\n\nFrom config/deadlines.yml (scmethyl-manuscript) — th
 e YAML is the source of truth\, this is a copy.
